 "sentences": [
  {
   "text": "Imagine waking up in July, expecting summer…",
   "t0": 0.0,
   "t1": 3.291
  },
  {
   "text": "only to find snow falling from the sky.",
   "t0": 4.028,
   "t1": 6.472
  },
  {
   "text": "In 1816, this really happened in parts of North America and Europe.",
   "t0": 6.981,
   "t1": 11.555
  },
  {
   "text": "But the cause was thousands of kilometres away.",
   "t0": 11.938,
   "t1": 14.757
  },
  {
   "text": "In April 1815, Mount Tambora, in present-day Indonesia, unleashed one of the most powerful volcanic eruptions ever recorded.",
   "t0": 15.198,
   "t1": 23.68
  },
  {
   "text": "The eruption sent enormous amounts of sulfur dioxide high into the atmosphere.",
   "t0": 24.1,
   "t1": 28.631
  },
  {
   "text": "There, it transformed into tiny sulfate aerosols, which spread through the air and reflected some incoming sunlight back into space.",
   "t0": 29.032,
   "t1": 36.729
  },
  {
   "text": "Less solar energy reached the surface.",
   "t0": 37.111,
   "t1": 39.432
  },
  {
   "text": "Temperatures fell, and weather patterns shifted.",
   "t0": 39.867,
   "t1": 42.42
  },
  {
   "text": "The effects were especially severe across parts of the Northern Hemisphere.",
   "t0": 42.9,
   "t1": 46.418
  },
  {
   "text": "In 1816, parts of Europe and North America experienced unusual cold, persistent rain, and even summer snowfall.",
   "t0": 46.839,
   "t1": 55.127
  },
  {
   "text": "Crops struggled, harvests failed, and food became harder to find.",
   "t0": 55.569,
   "t1": 60.046
  },
  {
   "text": "Communities faced hardship as food shortages and rising prices added to the crisis.",
   "t0": 60.477,
   "t1": 65.566
  },
  {
   "text": "A volcanic eruption thousands of kilometres away had consequences far beyond its birthplace.",
   "t0": 65.919,
   "t1": 71.886
  },
  {
   "text": "The year became known as the Year Without a Summer.",
   "t0": 72.337,
   "t1": 75.192
  },
  {
   "text": "It was a powerful reminder that one eruption can influence the climate far beyond the volcano itself.",
   "t0": 75.704,
   "t1": 81.711
  }
 ],
